      "Contraindicated in Child-Pugh C cirrhosis; no adjustment needed in Child-Pugh A or B without coagulopathy.",
      ["Landmark ARISTOTLE trial proven: ONLY DOAC to demonstrate superior stroke reduction, superior bleeding safety, AND a statistically significant reduction in all-cause mortality compared to warfarin", "Safest gastrointestinal bleeding profile among all direct oral anticoagulants", "Lowest renal clearance dependency (only 27%), making it the safest DOAC for chronic kidney disease and hemodialysis"],
